Shoalcade build fix for the Windows (MSVC) libretro core: the static C runtime (/MT) instead of the DLL one (/MD).
With /MD the core needs vcruntime140.dll and msvcp140.dll, which Windows does not have unless the Visual C++
Redistributable is installed, and Shoalcade's player loads cores that may import only Windows system DLLs
(tools/build_windows_cores.sh checks every core's imports). /MT links the runtime into xenia_edge_libretro.dll, so it
is one file, as every other Shoalcade core. Mesa (spirv_to_dxil, built by meson) is switched with it, so every library
in the link uses the same runtime. Checked builds (ASan) are left on the debug DLL runtime. No change to any other
platform.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 4eed30d42..ad0bb1aee 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@ if(MSVC)
   # CRT (/MD); Checked uses the debug CRT (/MDd) because it pairs /RTCsu
   # with ASan.
   set(CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY
-      "MultiThreaded$<$<CONFIG:Checked>:Debug>DLL"
+      "$<IF:$<CONFIG:Checked>,MultiThreadedDebugDLL,MultiThreaded>"
       CACHE STRING "" FORCE)
 
   # Patch the cached CMAKE_C/CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG so /MDd → /MD for Debug builds.
diff --git a/third_party/CMakeLists.txt b/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
index 471adb912..27a1b6f89 100644
--- a/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1140,7 +1140,7 @@ if(WIN32)
     # /MD matches xenia's CRT; /wd4189 overrides mesa's /we4189: Release strips
     # asserts, leaving assert-only locals that would trip the promoted warning.
     list(APPEND _xe_s2d_meson_args
-      -Db_vscrt=md -Dc_args=/wd4189 -Dcpp_args=/wd4189)
+      -Db_vscrt=mt -Dc_args=/wd4189 -Dcpp_args=/wd4189)
     if(NOT CMAKE_HOST_WIN32)
       # Cross-built from Linux with clang-cl (.ci/build-windows-cross.sh):
       # the script's clang-cl wrapper, which adds the target, lld and the CRT
